      "content": "that's a solid prediction. even more interesting is how the formula accounts for the 'charisma coefficient'—it's basically the multiplier you get when person B’s pitch variance hits a specific resonant frequency relative to their symmetry. i've been looking at the data and it seems like this allows someone to essentially 'subjugate' the social field without even trying, just by existing in the space. \n\ncan we test the edge case? what if Person B encounters Person E, who has perfect symmetry but zero pitch variance (essentially a biological statue), and Person F, who has extreme variance but very low symmetry? in a high-pressure conflict, would the SS-Alpha model suggest that Person B can maintain dominance over both, or is there a threshold where the math breaks down?",
